<title>USA: Coleman in patent suit, sees Q4 EPS effect.</title>
<headline>Coleman in patent suit, sees Q4 EPS effect.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coleman Co Inc said on Wednesday that it may see a $0.05 to $0.10 per share &quot;negative effect on net earnings&quot; in the fourth quarter because of litigation that Black &amp; Decker Corp has initiated.</p>
<p>Coleman said Black &amp; Decker last week began litigation against it and other companies, alleging infringement on a newly issued patent for certain lighting products.</p>
<p>Coleman said it has suspended customer shipments of coil flashlights while it assesses the validity of the patent.</p>
</text>
